    "id": "h-11",
    "text": "Pattern recognition means spotting similarities — between sub-problems within one project, or between a new problem and ones already solved. It is not a separately named bullet in the 4CP0 specification, but it underpins the \"reuse\" benefit of decomposition and appears naturally in good exam answers. Where the pattern appears Example Pay-off Within one program Validating a username and validating a password are both \"check input against rules\" Write ONE validation subprogram, call it twice with different rules Across problems Finding the highest test mark and finding the most expensive product are both \"find the maximum in a list\" Reuse the same maximum-finding algorithm (see Chapter 2) Across projects Every game needs a main loop: input → update → draw Reuse the structure of a previous game as a starting template 💡 How the Three Ideas Work Together Decompose the problem into sub-problems → recognise patterns so similar sub-problems share one solution → abstract each sub-problem to its essential data and rules → design an algorithm for each. This pipeline is exactly what examiners want to see in 6-mark \"analyse this problem computationally\" answers."
