    "id": "h-2",
    "text": "Computers constantly need to find an item in a collection of data (searching) and to arrange data into order (sorting). The exam expects you to know two searching algorithms and two sorting algorithms, to be able to follow them step by step, and to compare how efficient they are. 💡 Key Idea — Comparisons At GCSE we measure how efficient an algorithm is by counting the number of comparisons (or steps) it makes. Fewer comparisons = faster algorithm. You do not need Big-O notation for 4CP0."
