    "heading": "2. Linear Search [Spec 1.1.8]",
    "id": "h-3",
    "text": "🖼️ Image coming soon Figure 3.1 A linear search checks each item in turn from the start until the target is found or the list ends. assets/images/ch3-linear-search.png A linear search checks each item in the list one at a time, from the beginning, until it either finds the target or reaches the end. It is the simplest search and, importantly, works on lists that are not in order . # Linear search in Python def linear_search(data, target): for i in range(len(data)): if data[i] == target: return i # found — return the position return -1 # not found ⚡ EXAM TIP For a list of n items, a linear search makes at most n comparisons (the worst case is when the item is last, or not present at all). On average it checks about half the list."
