    "heading": "5. Bubble Sort [Spec 1.1.8]",
    "id": "h-7",
    "text": "A bubble sort compares each adjacent pair of items and swaps them if they are in the wrong order. After each full pass the largest remaining value has \"bubbled\" to the end. Passes repeat until a complete pass makes no swaps . 5.1 Worked Example — sort 5, 1, 4, 2, 8 Pass Comparisons and swaps Result Pass 1 (5,1)→swap, (5,4)→swap, (5,2)→swap, (5,8)→no swap 1, 4, 2, 5, 8 Pass 2 (1,4)→no, (4,2)→swap, (4,5)→no, (5,8)→no 1, 2, 4, 5, 8 Pass 3 No swaps made → list is sorted 1, 2, 4, 5, 8 ✓ # Bubble sort in Python def bubble_sort(data): n = len(data) swapped = True while swapped: swapped = False for i in range(n - 1): if data[i] > data[i + 1]: data[i], data[i + 1] = data[i + 1], data[i] swapped = True return data ⚠️ Common exam task You are often asked to show the list \"after one complete pass\" . Carry out every adjacent comparison for that single pass only — do not finish the whole sort."
