    "heading": "6. Emerging Trends in Computing [Spec 6.1.4]",
    "id": "h-17",
    "text": "The spec requires awareness of four current and emerging technologies: Trend What it is Potential impact Artificial intelligence (AI) Systems that learn from data and perform tasks that normally need human intelligence (recognising images, understanding speech, making predictions) Medical diagnosis, self-driving vehicles, recommendation systems — plus concerns about bias, jobs and accountability Quantum computing Computers using quantum bits (qubits) that can represent multiple states at once, solving certain problems exponentially faster Could crack today's encryption; could revolutionise drug design and optimisation problems DNA computing Using DNA molecules to perform massively parallel computation and to store data at extreme density Experimental — promises vast storage (an exabyte in a gram of DNA) and new ways to solve combinatorial problems Nanotechnology Engineering devices at the scale of nanometres (billionths of a metre) Ever-smaller, faster, more efficient chips; medical nanobots; new materials and sensors ⚡ EXAM TIP You need awareness , not deep technical detail: be able to name each trend, say in one sentence what it is, and give one possible impact on society."
